> 100% usage).
> 
> We've tried the following...
> 
> - quotacheck - does not work on clusters. I get the error "quotas are
> not
> supported in a cluster environment"
> - verify - I ran it offline. No change
> -defragment - no change
> 
> I've read that there is a "patched" version of quotacheck that WILL
> run on clusters.  Anyone know where I can get this patched version of
> quotacheck?  Or perhaps have a solution to our issue?
> 
> Thanks


Dorth,

The df command will show space on the disk that is not only used but
any space that is reserved by file processes.
The du command will show only the disk space being actually used.

Database programs like to preallocate space when a database is
opened/created to make sure that the space is there when it populates
it's own database / creates structures. That type of database usally
manages it's own data/files within that space and has variables to set
those limits.

Also know that the defalt behaviour of the OS with repect to free
space is that only root has write rights to a disk over 80% capasity.

Please visit to fuser command to determine which processes have files
open on that mount point.

Quincey


