Jeremy Thomson <panzerboy@gmail.com> wrote:
> I really need these directories cleared so that the vdump wont take so
> long.

Deleting files tends to be a slow operation with most UNIX file
systems, because each deletion involves updating metadata so it tends
to happen synchronously. I've also noticed that advfs is particularly
hard hit by large directories. There may not be a better solution. You
might consider putting these files on a UFS partition. UFS is also not
really fast at deleting, but it seems less out of control with large
directories.

If these files are REALLY temporary, you could replace the directories
with symlinks to a filesystem you just rebuild from scratch, or at least
don't vdump...

